Build the image file URL from the local path

The image dialog gave the local path to the URL constructor, which reads
the text as a URL. A per cent sign in the path became the start of an
escape. The file requester then showed the name of a file that does not
exist, and the configuration named that file.

Take the URL from QUrl::fromLocalFile, which keeps every character of
the path.

The change sits on the branch work/image-dialog of the local tree, as commit 4 of 5.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/config/imagepropertiesdialog.cpp b/qt6/config/imagepropertiesdialog.cpp
index a8b16e7a..6519425b 100644
--- a/qt6/config/imagepropertiesdialog.cpp
+++ b/qt6/config/imagepropertiesdialog.cpp
@@ -126,7 +126,7 @@ CImagePropertiesDialog::set(const QString &file, int width, int height,
         posCombo->setCurrentIndex(pos);
 
     fileRequester->setUrl(QFile::exists(file) && !QFileInfo(file).isDir() ?
-                          QUrl(file) : QUrl());
+                          QUrl::fromLocalFile(file) : QUrl());
 }
 
 QSize
